  abstract = {In recent years, many studies have aimed to use machine learning (ML) to improve the efficiency of large-scale structural analysis and topology optimization; nevertheless, robust generalization and high training and predictive accuracy remain difficult to achieve. This paper combines the generality of the substructure method with the high-accuracy advantages of operator-learning frameworks. Within a substructure-analysis setting, a Deep Operator Network (DeepONet) is trained to learn a high-fidelity mapping from a cubic B\'ezier interpolated boundary displacement field to the corresponding substructure's interior displacement field. This mapping depends solely on the material distribution within the substructure and admits a unique correspondence in theory. Numerical examples corroborate the effectiveness and stability of the proposed framework. Relative to the exact substructure method and to ML-enhanced variants that assume linear boundary displacements, the proposed approach strikes a favorable balance between efficiency and accuracy.},
